Adds a nullable family_id to item_price_schedules with a subject CHECK
(exactly one of item_id / family_id), a composite tenant foreign key to
item_families, family-scoped overlap exclusion guards mirroring the existing
item-scoped ones, and a family lookup index. No existing row is read,
rewritten, or deleted and no backfill runs: the column is new so no row can
match the family-keyed guards yet, every existing schedule is item-scoped so
the subject CHECK holds for all of them, and the untouched item-scoped
exclusions cannot collide with the new NULL item_id rows.
